From 0ac65ee5fecc32b8fd9f5ee4666231cc1bfa8b38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rocky <rocky@zeroclaw>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:15:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] feat(gateway): count spawn_subagent usage in the parent
 turn

A spawn_subagent child run has no event stream of its own, so its
TurnEvent::Usage (accepted responses, rejected billable attempts,
max-iteration summary attempts) was dropped and the parent's /ws/chat
done frame undercounted tokens and cost. All Usage emission sites now go
through UsageSink: the turn's own stream when it has one (unchanged),
otherwise the enclosing SubagentEventSink as TurnEvent::Subagent with
SubagentStep::Event(Usage). Never both.

/ws/chat folds a subagent Usage into input_tokens/output_tokens/
tokens_used and usage_by_provider (so cost_usd includes it), but not
into the accepted-serving snapshot: the context meter, last_* fields and
provider/model identity stay the parent turn's. The done frame gains
subagent_input_tokens/subagent_output_tokens (subset of the totals, null
without subagent usage). No ws frame is sent for the usage step itself.
ACP and RPC ignore Subagent events, so their counts are unchanged.
